NAME
    pager - present a file through the RumiAI technical pager abstraction

SYNOPSIS
    pager <file>

DESCRIPTION
    pager provides the technical paging boundary used by commands that need
    terminal presentation without embedding host-specific pager logic.

    Exactly one file operand is accepted. The file pathname is resolved through
    the runtime path-resolution facility and must identify a readable regular
    file.

    When standard output is not a terminal, pager copies the file directly to
    standard output so pipelines and redirections remain non-interactive.

    When standard output is a terminal, pager selects the viewer according to
    the current host policy.

HOST POLICY
    Linux
        Use less. The common util-linux more implementation does not provide the
        preferred bidirectional stay-at-end interaction in its normal host
        configuration.

        less is therefore a required Linux host capability for interactive
        paging. If it is unavailable, pager fails explicitly instead of falling
        back to the anomalous more behavior.

    Other hosts
        Use more until a concrete host divergence requires a dedicated adapter.

    When less is used, LESS, LESSOPEN and LESSCLOSE are neutralized for the
    viewer invocation so caller configuration does not silently alter pager
    behavior.

OPERANDS
    <file>
        Existing readable regular file to present.

EXIT STATUS
    0   Success.
    1   File resolution/access, required-backend availability or presentation
        failure.
    2   Invalid invocation.

SEE ALSO
